About the job
A global market-leader in digital fraud prevention and customer authentication, trusted by thousands of organizations worldwide, is seeking two temporary Sales Development Representatives (SDRs) for a 2–3 month contract to cover for a senior, seasoned rep who's moving on — that's why we're filling the gap with two people rather than one. Their products safeguard millions of accounts and billions of transactions annually — in short, you're the one stopping the crime. This is a great foot-in-the-door opportunity: you'll be joining a senior, high-earning sales team, learning from an experienced rep during your first week, and stepping into a company known for a strong culture.
In this role, you'll work closely with our Account Executive and Marketing teams to identify and engage decision-makers at financial institutions and payments companies, introduce them to their fraud prevention solutions, and turn those conversations into high-quality sales opportunities.
Compensation: $25/hr plus commission average per month $500 - $1,000 if doing wellAvailability: 100% remote. Hours will depend on your location — you'll need to train with someone in the Eastern time zone, so schedules run Monday–Friday, either 7:00am–4:00pm or 6:00am–3:00pmContract length: approximately 2–3 months, with the opportunity to interview for a permanent role if you perform well. Note: the company will also be actively recruiting externally for the permanent SDR position while temps are working, so strong performance gives you a shot — not a guarantee.
What you'll do
Prospect through outbound calls, emails, and social selling to reach decision-makers at financial institutions and payments companies
Follow up on a steady stream of warm leads — thanks to a recent run of webinars, you won't be starting every conversation cold
Partner with our Account Executives on account and territory strategy
Run discovery conversations to identify key decision-makers, understand their needs, and connect their challenges to our solutions
Qualify strong opportunities and hand them off to our Account Executive team with clear, actionable notes
Work from proven scripts and messaging — no need to build your pitch from scratch
Consistently hit activity, meeting, and pipeline-generation goals
Keep accurate records of your outreach and pipeline in Salesforce

What you bring
Bachelor's degree in Business, Marketing, Communications, or a related field — or equivalent experience
1–2+ years of sales, business development, or customer-facing experience is a plus, but not required — if you're eager to learn and break into sales, this is built for you
Genuine interest in building a career in enterprise technology, cybersecurity, fraud prevention, or SaaS sales
Curious and quick to pick up complex technology and business concepts
Comfort with cold calling, email prospecting, and social selling — you don't scare easily
Salesforce experience is a plus; experience with LinkedIn Sales Navigator or ZoomInfo is even better
Strong organization and time-management skills — this role is 100% remote, so you'll need to manage your own day well
Reliable, self-motivated, results-oriented, and open to coaching and feedback
Comfortable collaborating in a fast-paced, global team environment

Training & supportYou'll spend your first week training directly with a senior, experienced SDR to learn the ropes before working independently.
